        "4.2.notes.1": {
          "type": "line",
          "speaker": "NOTES",
          "delivery": "S",
          "emotion": "reading",
          "volume": "whisper",
          "text": "WHO'S ALLOWED. Fifteen with driver's ed. Fifteen and a half without. Somebody licensed in the seat next to you, always. The paper doesn't make you a driver. It means somebody agreed to watch.",
          "effects": {
            "unlock": [
              "fieldnotes.1"
            ],
            "log": "fieldnotes.read:1"
          },
          "next": "4.2.fail_end"
        },
        "4.2.notes.2": {
          "type": "line",
          "speaker": "NOTES",
          "delivery": "S",
          "emotion": "reading",
          "volume": "whisper",
          "text": "ON SIGNS. Red means stop. Yellow means somebody's worried. Orange means somebody's working, or was. Pennant on the left: don't pass. Nobody's maintaining them now. They're still right.",
          "effects": {
            "unlock": [
              "fieldnotes.2"
            ],
            "log": "fieldnotes.read:2"
          },
          "next": "4.2.fail_end"
        },
        "4.2.notes.3": {
          "type": "line",
          "speaker": "NOTES",
          "delivery": "S",
          "emotion": "reading",
          "volume": "whisper",
          "text": "ON GOING FIRST. Whoever stopped first. Same time, the one on the right. Turning left, everybody's ahead of you. Pedestrian, always. Nobody's coming. Do it anyway.",
          "effects": {
            "unlock": [
              "fieldnotes.3"
            ],
            "log": "fieldnotes.read:3"
          },
          "next": "4.2.fail_end"
        },
        "4.2.notes.4": {
          "type": "line",
          "speaker": "NOTES",
          "delivery": "S",
          "emotion": "reading",
          "volume": "whisper",
          "text": "ON LANES. Signal, mirror, shoulder, move. In that order. A hundred feet before, in town. Right lane's for driving. Left lane's for passing. Turn from the lane closest to where you're going, into the lane closest to where you came from.",
          "effects": {
            "unlock": [
              "fieldnotes.4"
            ],
            "log": "fieldnotes.read:4"
          },
          "next": "4.2.fail_end"
        },
        "4.2.notes.5": {
          "type": "line",
          "speaker": "NOTES",
          "delivery": "S",
          "emotion": "reading",
          "volume": "whisper",
          "text": "ON STOPPING. You don't stop where you brake. You stop where you brake plus where you were when you decided to. At sixty that's most of a football field. Pick a sign. Count three. Rain, four. Snow, don't be out there.",
          "effects": {
            "unlock": [
              "fieldnotes.5"
            ],
            "log": "fieldnotes.read:5"
          },
          "next": "4.2.fail_end"
        },
        "4.2.notes.6": {
          "type": "line",
          "speaker": "NOTES",
          "delivery": "S",
          "emotion": "reading",
          "volume": "whisper",
          "text": "ON SNOW. Everything gentle. Skid, foot off, steer where you want to go. Bridges freeze first. So does your judgment. Sign says chains, sign means chains.",
          "effects": {
            "unlock": [
              "fieldnotes.6"
            ],
            "log": "fieldnotes.read:6"
          },
          "next": "4.2.fail_end"
        },
        "4.2.notes.7": {
          "type": "line",
          "speaker": "NOTES",
          "delivery": "S",
          "emotion": "reading",
          "volume": "whisper",
          "text": "ON BIG RIGS. If you can't see the truck's mirrors, the truck can't see you. Don't hang out beside it. It turns wide. Lights on the shoulder, move over a lane. If you can't, slow down. That rule never changed.",
          "effects": {
            "unlock": [
              "fieldnotes.7"
            ],
            "log": "fieldnotes.read:7"
          },
          "next": "4.2.fail_end"
        },
        "4.2.notes.8": {
          "type": "line",
          "speaker": "NOTES",
          "delivery": "S",
          "emotion": "reading",
          "volume": "whisper",
          "text": "ON PASSENGERS. A distraction doesn't have to be loud to be dangerous. It just has to be interesting. Yes, the cat counts. Tired is a distraction too. Tired is quiet. It gets you before they do.",
          "effects": {
            "unlock": [
              "fieldnotes.8"
            ],
            "log": "fieldnotes.read:8"
          },
          "next": "4.2.fail_end"
        },
        "4.2.fail_end": {
